We are accepting applications for between one and four full-time
equivalent developer positions for work on a network security management
application.
This is an unexpected opportunity on a very tight schedule in response
to a potential research grant award.  Applications must be submitted no
later than August 4.  Initial selection will be made by August 9. 
Employment is contingent upon the grant award.  The award notification
should be September 2004.  Work commences in December or January.  The
grant is for sixth months but may develop into a permanent position.

Requirements include any of the following experience:
1) Mobile and embedded operating systems
2) iptables
3) socket programming
4) protocol development
5) GPS
6) Qt
7) User authentication systems

Details are posted in the Employment section on
http://www.opensourcedevelopmentcorp.com
Please follow the instructions carefully.
